On 2025-10-27 09:34:03 -0700 (-0700), Alan Coopersmith wrote:
[...]
>> The vendor was contacted early about this disclosure but did not=20
>> respond in any way.
[...]

With the flood of dubious reports being submitted by anyone who can=20
thumb some words into an LLM prompt and not bother to check the=20
results for hallucinated nonsense, I've taken to ignoring or=20
summarily closing such submissions to projects I work on as not=20
worth my time to respond. This is probably yet another sign that the=20
CVE system needs an overhaul or it's going to get ignored when it=20
becomes as overwhelmed with "AI noise" as everything else (not=20
saying these reports were necessarily machine-generated, but it's=20
reaching the point where open source projects with limited resources=20
have no choice but to silently bin such nonsense to /dev/null).
--=20
Jeremy Stanley

